Room: Room pages get //room's navigation throttle.

The host decides where each navigation of its pages goes before it starts
(the Engine protocol's decidePolicy: Peek opens an off-site link from a
pinned entry over the page, later space routing), and it needs to tell a
click on a link from a page's script setting window.location exactly
(backlog B-33; CEF could only guess from the status text). Both need a
content::NavigationThrottle on Room pages: the NavigationHandle has the
transition, the gesture, WasInitiatedByLinkClick() and the redirects, and a
throttle can cancel synchronously at WillStartRequest.

No existing hook: throttles are added only by the ContentBrowserClient
(ChromeContentBrowserClient::CreateThrottlesForNavigation, which calls
CreateAndAddChromeThrottlesForNavigation and nothing an embedder can
extend); NavigationHandle::RegisterThrottleForTesting is test-only;
WebContentsObserver::DidStartNavigation cannot cancel. A
ContentBrowserClient subclass would mean replacing Chrome's for one call.
//room adds its throttle last (it never defers) and only for the primary
main frame of a page RoomCore wraps.

Phase 3.3a, 2026-10-05. //room: room/core/room_web_contents.mm
(InstallWebContentsHooks, RoomNavigationThrottle).
diff --git a/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client_navigation_throttles.cc b/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client_navigation_throttles.cc
index ce3cc119e6c3c..4756fb9c08450 100644
